## F9+ (post-F8)

### F9 — ThemeProviderChain vs CSS precedence

**Problem:** operator dark toggle sets `html.dark` and `ThemeProviderChain`’s inner `.theme-dark`. Platform `globals.css` / design-token theme layers can assign platform blue to `.theme-dark`, overriding body-scoped Denali DTCG vars for shell children (see [`admin-experience.md`](../workspaces/denali/admin-experience.md) § Dark mode cascade).

**Contract (already partial in `admin-skin.css`):**

1. `html.dark:has(body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"])` — document root + portals
2. `body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"] .theme-dark` — provider subtree inside shell

**F9 deliverables:**

| Step | Work |
| ---- | ---- |
| F9-1 | Audit: enumerate all `.theme-dark` / `ThemeProviderChain` inline vars that conflict with `admin-semantic-tokens.css` | ✅ (see § F9-1 audit below) |
| F9-2 | Guard or spec: Denali admin primary in dark mode ≠ platform `#5b9fd4` (extend `denali-admin-theme` or Playwright `SMK-P9-DENALI-THEME`) | ✅ `guard-denali-admin-dark-primary` · `WEB-DENALI-THEME-14` · `SMK-P9-DENALI-THEME` |
| F9-3 | Doc closure: precedence table in `dtcg-pipeline-spec` + `platform-architecture-v2` | ✅ (see § F9-3 below) |
| F9-4 | C4 remediation: tenant inline `--color-primary` deferred in dark mode | ✅ `TenantThemeProvider` + `buildTenantThemeStyle({ omitPrimaryColor })` |

#### F9-1 audit — ThemeProviderChain vs Denali admin semantics (2026-07-06)

**DOM chain** (`ThemeProviderChain` → operator shell):

```text
body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"][data-app-surface="admin"]
└─ PlatformThemeProvider → div.theme-dark | div.theme-light     ← toggle target
   └─ TenantThemeProvider → div[data-tenant-theme] style=inline --color-primary* (light only; omitted when html.dark per F9-4)
      └─ WorkspaceThemeProvider → div[data-workspace-theme] style=workspace cssVariables
         └─ operator shell + feature children (shadcn, Radix portals)
```

Operator dark toggle (`operator-theme-mode.ts`) writes **both** `html.dark` on `<html>` and `theme-dark` on the `PlatformThemeProvider` root (same contract as Playwright `SMK-P9-DENALI-THEME`).

**Admin CSS load order** (via `apps/web/app/globals.css` → `admin-bootstrap.css`):

| # | File | `.theme-dark` role |
| - | ---- | ------------------ |
| 1 | `index.css` → `themes/dark.css` | Platform palette on `.theme-dark` — `--color-primary: #5b9fd4` |
| 2 | `shell-bridge.css` | shadcn aliases `--primary`, `--sidebar-primary` → `var(--color-primary)` |
| 3 | `operator-admin-dark-semantics.css` | Duplicate platform dark palette on `.theme-dark`, `.dark` |
| 4 | `denali-admin.css` → `admin-semantic-tokens.css` | Denali DTCG dark block on triple cascade (below) |

**Denali dark authority selector** (`denali.admin.tokens.json` block 2 → `admin-semantic-tokens.css`):

```text
html.dark:has(body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"]),
.dark body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"],
body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"] .theme-dark
```

Without the third arm, shadcn `bg-primary` inside `div.theme-dark` keeps platform `#5b9fd4` even when `body` exposes teal `--primary` via the first two arms only.

**Conflict inventory**

| ID | Source | Mechanism | Dark value (platform) | Denali authority | Severity | Mitigation today |
| -- | ------ | --------- | --------------------- | ---------------- | -------- | ---------------- |
| C1 | `themes/dark.css` | `.theme-dark { --color-primary }` | `#5b9fd4` | `#5eead4` | **P0** | Triple cascade on `.theme-dark` div (specificity 0,2,1) |
| C2 | `operator-admin-dark-semantics.css` | `.theme-dark`, `.dark` full palette | platform GitHub dark | Denali forest dark | **P0** for primary | Same as C1; file is platform admin fallback — Denali skin loads after bootstrap |
| C3 | `shell-bridge.css` | `.theme-dark { --primary: var(--color-primary) }` | aliases C1 | `{flat.primary}` in DTCG | **P0** | Denali flat aliases in semantic block override `--primary` on matched selector |
| C4 | `TenantThemeProvider` | inline `style` on `[data-tenant-theme]` | `--color-primary` from tenant DB (`#0f766e` default) | dark `#5eead4` | **P1** | **F9-4:** omit `primaryColor` inline mapping when `html.dark` (`useDocumentDarkMode` in theme-react) |
| C5 | `WorkspaceThemeProvider` | inline `style` on `[data-workspace-theme]` | workspace `cssVariables` / `tokens.css` | admin semantic block | **P2** | Usually defers to `--ws-color-accent`; admin semantic sets shadcn `--accent` |
| C6 | `themes/dark.css` + `operator-admin-dark-semantics.css` | status tokens not in Denali dark DTCG block | `--color-danger` `#ff7b72`, `--color-success` `#56d364`, `--color-warning` `#e3b341`, `--color-info` `#79c0ff` | light-block only in `denali.admin.tokens.json` | **P2** | No Denali dark override — destructive/warning/success badges use platform GitHub hues |
| C7 | `ui-primitives/Select/select-affordance.css` | `.theme-dark [data-ui-select]` chevron stroke | `#a8b0a4` | cosmetic | **P3** | Decorative SVG stroke only |

**React providers — inline vars set on chain** (`packages/theme-react`):

| Provider | Inline keys | Conflicts with admin semantic |
| -------- | ----------- | ------------------------------ |
| `PlatformThemeProvider` | none (class only) | — |
| `TenantThemeProvider` | `--color-primary`, `--color-primary-hover`, `--color-text-link`, tenant `cssVariables` | **C4** ✅ F9-4 — primary family omitted when `html.dark` |
| `WorkspaceThemeProvider` | normalized `workspaceTheme.cssVariables` | **C5** — accent/brand overrides |

**Open remediation (post-F9-4):**

1. **C6:** extend `denali.admin.tokens.json` dark block with `color.danger|success|warning|info` (+ `flat.destructive`) or accept platform status hues.
2. **C1–C3 long-term:** gate platform `.theme-dark` palette behind non-Denali body (`:not(:has(body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"]))`) in generated CSS — requires DTCG generator change (Phase G adjacency).

**Closed:** C4 — F9-4 `omitPrimaryColor` in `TenantThemeProvider` / `buildTenantThemeStyle`.

#### F9-3 — CSS precedence table (admin dark mode)

When multiple layers set the same custom property, **higher priority wins** for descendants. Denali admin requires the triple cascade (F9-1) so layer 2 beats layers 3–5 on `div.theme-dark`.

| Priority | Layer | Selector / scope | Applies to | Overrides |
| -------- | ----- | ---------------- | ---------- | --------- |
| 1 | Inline React style | `[data-tenant-theme]`, `[data-workspace-theme]` | Tenant / workspace subtree | Parent-inherited CSS vars on descendants[^c4] |
| 2 | Denali admin DTCG | `html.dark:has(body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"])`, `.dark body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"]`, `body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"] .theme-dark` | Body, portals, `PlatformThemeProvider` root | Platform `.theme-dark` palette (C1–C3) |
| 3 | Platform admin dark semantics | `.theme-dark`, `.dark` in `operator-admin-dark-semantics.css` | Non-Denali admin fallback | `themes/dark.css` where duplicated |
| 4 | Platform theme | `.theme-dark` in `themes/dark.css` | All `ThemeProviderChain` dark subtrees | — |
| 5 | shadcn bridge | `:root`, `.theme-dark` in `shell-bridge.css` | Tailwind `@theme inline` aliases | Maps to `--color-*` from layers above |

[^c4]: **C4 (F9-4 mitigated):** `TenantThemeProvider` skips inline `--color-primary*` when `html.dark` so Denali dark semantic cascade applies to the tenant subtree. Wizard still re-binds `[data-new-tour-wizard]` in `wizard-skin.css` as belt-and-suspenders.

